        "@value": "A reference to metrics related to package such as OpenSSF scorecards."
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label": [
      {
        "@value": "metrics"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Dataset/DatasetAvailabilityType",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Availability of dataset."
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/ExternalIdentifierType/isci",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual",
      "https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/ExternalIdentifierType"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "International Standard Collection Identifier (ISCI) is a variable-length identifier standardized by [ISO 27730](https://www.iso.org/standard/44293.html) for identifying collections held by libraries, archives, museums, and other memory institutions. It consists of two parts: the identifier for the assigning organization (an ISIL) enclosed in square brackets, followed by a local collection identifier string (e.g., `[FR-751041001]Casadesus1`)."
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label": [
      {
        "@value": "isci"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/IsoAutomationLevel/conditionalAutomation",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual",
      "https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/IsoAutomationLevel"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Level 3 - Conditional automation. The system can propose strategies and then automatically execute the approved plan, with an external agent being ready to take over when necessary."
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label": [
      {
        "@value": "conditionalAutomation"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Operations/exportControlSpecification",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Specification basis for the export control classification."
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range": [
      {
        "@id": "https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/Specification"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/review",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual",
      "https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/FunctionalSafety/VerificationType"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "A examination or checking of documentation, records, processes, or systems to confirm compliance or adherence with an upper level requirement. Typically done as peer review, offline review or review meeting."
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label": [
      {
        "@value": "review"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Software/SoftwarePurpose/evidence",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual",
      "https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Software/SoftwarePurpose"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "The Element is the evidence that a specification or requirement has been fulfilled."
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label": [
      {
        "@value": "evidence"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Software/ContentIdentifierType/gitoid",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual",
      "https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Software/ContentIdentifierType"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "[Gitoid](https://www.iana.org/assignments/uri-schemes/prov/gitoid), stands for [Git Object ID](https://git-scm.com/book/en/v2/Git-Internals-Git-Objects). A gitoid of type blob is a unique hash of a binary artifact. A gitoid may represent either an [Artifact Identifier](https://github.com/omnibor/spec/blob/eb1ee5c961c16215eb8709b2975d193a2007a35d/spec/SPEC.md#artifact-identifier-types) for the software artifact or an [Input Manifest Identifier](https://github.com/omnibor/spec/blob/eb1ee5c961c16215eb8709b2975d193a2007a35d/spec/SPEC.md#input-manifest-identifier) for the software artifact's associated [Artifact Input Manifest](https://github.com/omnibor/spec/blob/eb1ee5c961c16215eb8709b2975d193a2007a35d/spec/SPEC.md#artifact-input-manifest); this ambiguity exists because the Artifact Input Manifest is itself an artifact, and the gitoid of that artifact is its valid identifier. Gitoids calculated on software artifacts (Snippet, File, or Package Elements) should be recorded in the SPDX 3 SoftwareArtifact's contentIdentifier property. Gitoids calculated on the Artifact Input Manifest (Input Manifest Identifier) should be recorded in the SPDX 3 Element's externalIdentifier property. See [OmniBOR Specification](https://github.com/omnibor/spec/), a minimalistic specification for describing software [Artifact Dependency Graphs](https://github.com/omnibor/spec/blob/eb1ee5c961c16215eb8709b2975d193a2007a35d/spec/SPEC.md#artifact-dependency-graph-adg)."
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label": [
      {
        "@value": "gitoid"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Security/VulnAssessmentRelationship",
